KG42.register("source_edge_archive-d71e409d8f8ae90ac422a5cc",{"id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E001","paper":"13-consensus_product_differentiation","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","rule_ref":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R003","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E001","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"clearing.social_welfare","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e31","v141-b-g03-E15"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-fe1c33d7a61b4b97","target":"KG31-95bb253080ce87de","source_occurrence_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","target_occurrence_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R003::V::clearing.social_welfare","source_unit_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::M01::coordination.price_signal","target_unit_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::M01::clearing.social_welfare","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Decentralized RCI implementation of the MBED market for the community of agents. | MBED optimization over the community of agents and their bilateral trading quantities.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e31","v141-b-g03-E15"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"b740baf77528bb8204fa598bcc8ae435f9fe58a292f453f14fe3f6200136f252","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"M01","source_definition":"The producer's current offered bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a producer's bilateral quantity. The consumer's current requested bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a consumer's bilateral quantity. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the producer's current offered bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Producer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a producer and its communication neighbor. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the consumer's current requested bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Consumer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a consumer and its communication neighbor. Each agent must send its bilateral price estimate to its communication neighbor as part of the prescribed information exchange. Scope: Per-iteration communication between neighboring agents in RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration. The participants' separately calculated price estimates for a given bilateral trade must agree, λ_nm = λ_mn. Scope: Individually calculated price estimates for the same bilateral trade in the fully decentralized RCI implementation. Condition: After convergence. Reaching optimality through RCI does not require sharing agents' internal production/consumption parameters or product-differentiation criterion parameters. Scope: Information disclosure in the RCI implementation of MBED. The iterative process stops when convergence is established; convergence criterion (26) is optional. Scope: Termination of iterative RCI coordination. Condition: When algorithmic convergence is established under the prescribed stopping criteria.","target_definition":"Distributed RCI price-signal coordination provides a decentralized implementation of the MBED social-welfare clearing problem. Scope: Decentralized RCI implementation of the MBED market for the community of agents. The MBED clearing objective maximizes community social welfare by minimizing aggregate agent costs plus bilateral trading costs, subject to each agent's power-injection bounds, role-dependent sign constraints and bilateral reciprocity constraints. Scope: MBED optimization over the community of agents and their bilateral trading quantities.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Distributed RCI price-signal coordination provides a decentralized implementation of the MBED social-welfare clearing problem. Scope: Decentralized RCI implementation of the MBED market for the community of agents.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","clearing.social_welfare"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e31","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g01-e21","v141-b-g01-e33"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":"996","section":"II-C. MBED Formulation","anchor_text":"of resented by a unique balance constraint in a classic pool-based model. It is here replaced by a s","equation_id":"(9a), (9b)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The Multi-Bilateral Economic Dispatch optimization problem has for objective to maximize the social welfare of the community of agents (9a) under the constraints of each agent's power injection limits (9b) and sign constraints (9d)–(9e) as well as the reciprocity constraints (9c). This reads min_D Σ_{n∈Ω} (C_n(P_n) + C̃_n(p_n)) (9a) s.t. P_n ≤ P_n ≤ P̄_n ∀n ∈ Ω (9b)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e31","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-B. Dual Updates","anchor_text":"sists in updating the decision variables based on a gradient step im built on optimality conditions ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Compared to the dual decomposition of [18], the algorithm is here implemented in a fully decentralized setup. The consequence is that price estimates for a given trade are also calculated individually by each participant, even though after convergence, a consensus has to be reached on these estimates (i.e., λ_nm = λ_mn). This convergence of price estimates is ensured in the price update, (11), through a consensus term. The last term, the innovation term, ensures the enforcement of the equality constraint (as in the dual ascent method)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p09-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":9,"printed_page":"1002","section":"V. Conclusion and Perspectives","anchor_text":"should be adapted to a hybrid multi bilateral and pool based eco nomic dispatch to improve efﬁciency","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Acknowledging increasing available flexibility of consumers and prosumers, as well as the increasingly decentralized nature of power generation, we have proposed a structure for peer-to-peer electricity markets, based on multi-bilateral trading and product differentiation. We showed that the MBED market framework can be easily and efficiently implemented without the need of a central agent through a distributed Relaxed Consensus+Innovation approach with only a limited exchange of information. This RCI implementation was shown to solve the MBED problem with acceptable optimality gap."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e21","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p04-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":"997","section":"II-C. MBED Formulation","anchor_text":"TY MARKETS WITH PRODUCT DIFFERENTIATION 997 c) for a decentralized implementation of the MBED using ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"This means that in practice, through the decentralized solution approach described in the following, all involved agents focus only on solving their own local profit maximization (or cost minimization) problem, regardless of overall social welfare. It is by construction, and only by construction, that we know that each agent concentrating on solving their own local problem will yield maximum social welfare solution at convergence. In other words, there is no structural gap between the solutions of the centralized and decentralized approaches to solving the MBED problem, and hence no price to pay for reaching consensus over obtaining the most efficient market outcome."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e33","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-A. Structure of the Method","anchor_text":"prFig. 2. Flowchart of the relaxed consensus + innovation algorithm. from the others. This results i","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 2","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"An iteration of the Relaxed Consensus + Innovation method can be split into three steps. The first two steps consist in updating the dual variables of the trading reciprocity constraints and of the power boundary constraints (III-B). The third step consists in updating the decision variables based on a gradient step built on optimality conditions of the local optimality problem (III-C). Some operational aspects are presented in III-D. The structure of the algorithm is summed up in Fig. 2."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Decentralized RCI implementation of the MBED market for the community of agents. | MBED optimization over the community of agents and their bilateral trading quantities.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e31","v141-b-g03-E15"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E001","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"clearing.social_welfare","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e31","v141-b-g03-E15"]},"paper_scope_note":"The λ update, P update, and required communication of RCI have direct formula basis; only protocol component dependencies are allowed, and the values of k and k+1 or the roles of consumer and producer are not conflated."}});
